# Auto-sync to GitHub

After **any** `git commit` in this repository:

1. Immediately run `git push -u origin HEAD` (or push the current branch to `origin`).
2. Confirm the branch is **not** still `ahead of origin` before ending the turn.
3. Never leave commits local-only — unpushed work was lost before when the disk was wiped.

The repo also has `.githooks/post-commit` and Cursor hooks that auto-push; still verify push succeeded if anything looks offline.
